# Oath of Druids triggers at "each player's upkeep", comparing creature counts with the player whose upkeep it is, not
# with the Oath's controller. Bot1 casts the Oath and a Llanowar Elves on turn 1. At Bot2's upkeep on turn 2 Bot2 controls
# fewer creatures than its opponent, so it is the one to reveal: two Forests go to its graveyard and an Elvish Mystic onto its
# battlefield. At Bot1's upkeep on turn 3 each player controls one creature, so the target (a player who controls MORE) does
# not exist and nothing triggers (the stack is empty and Bot1's library is untouched).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Oath of Druids
Llanowar Elves
Swamp
Swamp
Island x3
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Forest
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Swamp x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oath of Druids.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot2.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
? Bot2.Graveyard = Forest; Forest
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Library.Count = 12

